# {{BRAND_TITLE}} — {{REPO_NAME}} (Spring-BFF, NON-BUILDABLE placeholder skeleton)

> **This is NOT a runnable service.** Base-absent fallback for the mesh
> repo-templating **spring-bff** archetype. A Snapdragon BFF is a **compiled
> Spring Boot 4 / Java** service — unlike the angular-mfe static bundle it has
> **no faithful minimal boot**, so there is deliberately no vendored source here.
>
> Two-tier fallback guarantee for this archetype: **"never refuses"** holds (a
> tree is always emitted); **"bootable"** does NOT (a compiled BFF cannot be
> stubbed into a running jar). See docs/MESH-TEMPLATING.md, per-archetype
> skeleton note.

`render-tenant-set.sh` renders this placeholder only so it never *refuses* when
the Tier-2 base cannot be pulled. The read-only base (`snapdragon-{{REPO_NAME}}`
@ the org's GitLab/GitHub) is REQUIRED to produce a real, buildable tenant tree.

To emit a real tree, make the base resolvable and re-run:

```
scripts/render-repo-tree.sh <brand.conf> --enable-repo-tree --repo {{REPO_NAME}} --archetype spring-bff
```

The archetype recipe then anchor-edits the brand-coupled `application.yml`
env-defaults + the `.gitlab-ci.yml` include onto the pulled base.
